    "notes": "Standard 70 Shore A peroxide-cured EPDM (ethylene propylene diene monomer rubber) compound. Peroxide cure provides higher temperature resistance (to +150°C) compared to sulfur cure (to +125°C). EPDM is incompatible with petroleum oils and greases — do not use in contact with mineral oils, gasoline, or diesel. Excellent ozone, UV, and weathering resistance. Thermal diffusivity is derived from thermal conductivity (k), density (ρ), and specific heat (Cp) — not an independently measured value."
